{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791564224,"nonce":"UPbHhbgAp1yk8O7x5TtdHcfYBDU=","title":"Retire stateful closures: what they stand in for, and the property-channel gaps behind them","message":"Direction: get rid of stateful closures as far as possible. ashui needs none; it relies on property bindings and signals only (6f7b001, points 4 and 5). This issue holds what was measured and the order to do it in. Public builder signatures stay as they are: they already take Reactive\u003cT\u003e.\n\nMeasured (non-test source, workspace crates and examples):\n- .on_state( 144 sites: blinc_layout 63, blinc_app_examples 47, blinc_cn 31, others 3.\n- use_state_keyed( 190, .deps( 97, StateTransitions 75. stateful.rs is 5,742 lines.\n\nWhat the closures do. The 144 cannot be classified by a script: a closure returns a Div that is merged onto a base, so style-only and structural bodies look alike. Reading the cn sites instead:\n- Almost none select a hover or press style. They are \"a signal changed, rebuild this subtree\": the popover trigger follows open_state, the collapsible body follows is_open, the slider's value text is a signal formatted to a string, and cn's reactive_props::reactive_node wraps a Stateful so a bound label or image rebuilds on every change.\n- The large ones (tree 284 lines, number_input 239, sidebar 216, pagination 203) are structural.\n- Rebuilt content runs after the stylesheet pass, so it can lose CSS inheritance and render unstyled until another pass runs; reactive_node's own doc comment warns about this. In-place updates do not have that hazard.\n\nSo the missing piece is not a pseudo-class replacement. It is the content and structure primitives ashui has.\n\nThe property channel is partly built. Verified by grep for the writers: Background, Opacity, CornerRadius, Width, Padding, Gap, Transform and Shadow have them. Display, FlexDirection, FontSize, text Color, Overflow and TextContent are declared in PropertyId and written nowhere. cn's button says so itself: a bound label rebuilds the subtree because TextContent is \"declared but unimplemented\". SideEffects::needs_text_remeasure is computed but nothing reads it.\n\nOrder:\n0. One drain. The loop that applies queued render and layout writes was copied six times across four runners (windowed twice, web twice, iOS, Android). It is now RenderTree::apply_partial_property_updates. Done.\n1. A TextContent write: a third write kind in that one drain, updating the node's measure context and its text data, with needs_text_remeasure acted on. Plus a Text constructor taking a Reactive\u003cString\u003e, additive.\n2. Writers for Display (show and hide) and the text style properties.\n3. Move the cn sites that are only a display onto those: the slider value, reactive_node's labels, the button label.\n4. Interaction state as per-node signals (hovered, pressed, focused, disabled, ...) so a state variant is a computed over them. Meets 7cabafe: a variant writes at the stylesheet tier.\n5. Structural primitives, show and for, with persistent nodes and owner scopes. Depends on the identity work (StableNodeId, 6f7b001 \"Identity reconstruction\"). This is where the 200-line closures go. The DSL already has with blocks and List\u003cT\u003e.\n\nKeep: the state machine facility, for logic. What goes is using one to choose a style.","files":null}]}